Question: Which Flutter layout widgets would you use to structure this card so it looks consistent across screen sizes? Explain how 
MediaQuery, Expanded or Flexible can be used to replace fixed pixel dimensions and make the card responsive.

Answer:
I would use Card, Column, Row, Expanded and Flexible to create a responsive restaurant card.
-> Card: Provides the restaurant card design.

-> Column: Arranges the image, restaurant name and cuisine vertically.

-> Row: Places the text and “Order Now” button horizontally.

-> MediaQuery: Gets the screen size to adjust the card dimensions according to the device.

-> Expanded and Flexible: Distribute available space and prevent text or images from stretching awkwardly.

Instead of fixed pixel dimensions I would use screen width and flexible layouts to ensure the restaurant card looks consistent on both 
small and large screens.
